From: patrickjquinn <patrick.jm.quinn@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 08:35:40 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 250/250] arm64: configs: mt6858: Turn lockups and RCU stalls
 into panics

The JP2601 runs systemd's hardware watchdog with a 15 s timeout, so a
stuck kernel shows up only as a silent reset. Build the soft- and
hard-lockup (buddy) detectors with panic on detection, and bring the
RCU stall timeout down from 21 s to 10 s, so a hang panics and leaves
its oops in pstore (the ramoops region LK reserves) before the watchdog
resets the board.
---
 arch/arm64/configs/mt6858.config | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/configs/mt6858.config b/arch/arm64/configs/mt6858.config
index f51e3fe41..95730670c 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/configs/mt6858.config
+++ b/arch/arm64/configs/mt6858.config
@@ -102,3 +102,10 @@ CONFIG_RTC_DRV_MT6397=y
 # SoC temperatures from the LVTS sensors, for thermal throttling.
 CONFIG_MTK_THERMAL=y
 CONFIG_MTK_LVTS_THERMAL=y
+# A hang panics into pstore (LK's ramoops) before the 15 s hardware
+# watchdog bites, instead of a silent reset.
+CONFIG_SOFTLOCKUP_DETECTOR=y
+CONFIG_BOOTPARAM_SOFTLOCKUP_PANIC=y
+CONFIG_HARDLOCKUP_DETECTOR=y
+CONFIG_BOOTPARAM_HARDLOCKUP_PANIC=y
+CONFIG_RCU_CPU_STALL_TIMEOUT=10
